			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Unshadow logger:getLevel handler from broad NOOP arm\n\nlogger:getLevel was matched by a broad logger:* + setVisibility => Ok(Value::Null)\narm before the dedicated handler (returning log::max_level() as u32) was reached.\nRemove logger:getLevel from the NOOP arm so the dedicated handler can execute.\nVS Code's LogLevel API now receives the correct numeric value.",
			"SHA": "0a7c3ddeb29c720a1794413424713be12baa38df"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T17:36:48Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1855,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add glob normalization to FindInFiles, realign README template\n\nAdd `NormalizeGlobArgument` helper that normalizes include/exclude arguments\nin `FindInFiles` — accepting either a single glob string or `string[]` — and\nplumb `maxResults` from the 6th positional argument. Rename `isRegex` to\n`isRegExp` to match the VS Code search contract, and extract the trailing\noptions `Value` from remaining arguments instead of consuming only the first\npositional object.\n\nOverhaul the `README.md` with the standardized Land element documentation\ntemplate: combine technology icon badges with crate/version badges using\nem-quad spacing, simplify tables to bare pipe-only format, add a\nCompatibility section documenting inter-element gRPC and IPC dependencies,\nremove the duplicate NLnet funding paragraph, fix Mermaid diagram entity\nencoding (`&amp;` → `&`), and align heading terminology and list formatting\nwith Land conventions.",
			"SHA": "4a291a9c6e8083e6c6d15cb21c47330c48215e40"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T17:23:34Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1855,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Harden boot init — cache machine ID, fallible URL construction, defensive windowId\n\nThree defensive hardening changes to `InitializationData` that prevent panics during rapid development restarts and eliminate a redundant disk read per boot.\n\nWrap the machine ID in a `OnceLock` so the second caller per boot (the extension-host init-data path) reads from memory instead of re-opening `machine-id.txt`.\n\nReplace the bare `unwrap()` on `ApplicationHandle.get_webview_window(\"main\")` with a `map`/`unwrap_or_else` fallback to `\"main\"`. During rapid Tauri restarts the webview window may not yet be registered, and this value is only a label sent to the frontend — a string default is harmless where a panic would abort the entire boot sequence.\n\nExtract `url::Url::from_directory_path` into a fallible `DirectoryUrl` helper that propagates via `CommonError::ConfigurationLoad` instead of calling `unwrap()`. Relative paths (common in dev environments without a real app bundle) previously panicked at all four call sites for `appRoot`, `globalStorageHome`, `workspaceStorageHome`, and `logsLocation`.\n\nNo behavioural change on production bundles where all paths are absolute and windows exist — the same values are produced, just without the panic risk on edge cases.",
			"SHA": "8a9d7aa4844bc79a9847d17d6e9c10ad969ad7a1"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T17:22:09Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1855,
				2
			],
			"Message": "perf(Mountain): Parallelize PostSetup boot stages, cache machine-id read\n\nThe sequential PostSetup lifecycle — config pass 1, extension scan, config re-merge, Vine gRPC bind, Cocoon start, Air start — wasted wall-clock time running independent work serially. The machine-ID file was also read from disk twice (sandbox config + extension-host init data) with no cache.\n\nRestructure the boot pipeline into three parallel stages using `tokio::join!`:\n- Stage 1: configuration pass 1 ∥ extension scan (no mutual dependency)\n- Stage 2: configuration re-merge (requires finished scan) ∥ Vine gRPC server bind (depends on neither)\n- Stage 3: Cocoon ∥ Air sidecar starts (both connect to Vine, neither depends on the other)\n\nAdd a `DirsReady` await before the first config merge so the background userdata-dir task has finished writing defaults and the trust-key injection before settings.json is read.\n\nCache the persistent machine ID in a `OnceLock` inside `InitializationData` so `ConstructSandboxConfiguration` and `ConstructExtensionHostInitializationData` read the file once per boot instead of twice.\n\nReduces the serialised boot path and eliminates one redundant disk read.",
			"SHA": "e0c0c055d1e36c19a16aa70fe7fbab0b4d8c603e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T17:20:10Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1855,
				15
			],
			"Message": "perf(Mountain): Offload dir setup to blocking pool, wire 13 more providers to RunCancellable\n\nMove the 14 `create_dir_all` calls, default-file writes, and settings.json trust-key injection from synchronous inline code into `tauri::async_runtime::spawn_blocking` so boot-time filesystem IO runs concurrently with the rest of PostSetup. The memento hydration path remains synchronous because the webview's first `storage:getItems` depends on the hydrated in-memory map being present before configuration merge.\n\nSwitch the `vscode-resource://` scheme handler from `std::thread::spawn` (~100µs overhead per request) to `tauri::async_runtime::spawn_blocking`, consistent with the `vscode-file://` handler migrated in the previous commit.\n\nWire 13 language feature providers — document highlights, document range formatting, folding ranges, inline completion items, linked editing ranges, on-type formatting, rename edits, selection ranges, workspace symbols, prepare call hierarchy, prepare type hierarchy, type hierarchy subtypes, and type hierarchy supertypes — through `Service.RunCancellable`. Each now races its environment forward against a cancellation token and returns a default empty response on cancel instead of blocking on the forward.\n\nCompletes the RunCancellable coverage for all language feature providers in CocoonServiceImpl, eliminating the worst-case main-thread stall from directory creation and making all 25+ provider endpoints responsive to cancellation.",
			"SHA": "6edbbd014f68f102c9a9133468e4f61b7991074d"
		}
	],
